1
00:01:22,548 --> 00:01:25,108
<i>They are an army unlike any other...</i>

2
00:01:25,184 --> 00:01:29,018
<i>crusading across the stars
toward a place called UnderVerse,</i>

3
00:01:29,087 --> 00:01:31,021
<i>their promised land...</i>

4
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:34,388
<i>a constellation of dark new worlds.</i>

5
00:01:34,459 --> 00:01:36,893
<i>Necromongers, they're called.</i>

6
00:01:36,962 --> 00:01:41,331
<i>And if they cannot convert you,
they will kill you.</i>

7
00:01:42,935 --> 00:01:45,994
<i>Leading them, the Lord Marshal.</i>

8
00:01:46,071 --> 00:01:50,131
<i>He alone has made a pilgrimage
to the gates of the UnderVerse...</i>

9
00:01:50,209 --> 00:01:53,440
<i>and returned a different being.</i>

10
00:01:53,512 --> 00:01:56,777
<i>Stronger. Stranger.</i>

11
00:01:56,849 --> 00:02:00,147
<i>Half alive and half...</i>

12
00:02:00,218 --> 00:02:02,949
<i>something else.</i>

13
00:02:13,531 --> 00:02:17,558
<i>If we are to survive,
a new balance must be found.</i>

14
00:02:18,636 --> 00:02:21,571
<i>In normal times,
evil would be fought by good.</i>

15
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,631
<i>But in times like these, well,</i>

16
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:27,873
<i>it should be fought
by another kind of evil.</i>

17
00:03:01,846 --> 00:03:06,249
Linin' him up for you. Port-side
shot comin' up. Steady. Here we go.

18
00:03:13,492 --> 00:03:16,290
Steady.

19
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:19,387
<i>Take it. Take it!</i>

20
00:03:19,464 --> 00:03:21,898
Take the shot!

21
00:03:24,003 --> 00:03:26,630
Shit!
Toombs, we're runnin' out of road!

22
00:03:26,705 --> 00:03:28,899
Shut up! I got it! Again!

23
00:03:31,443 --> 00:03:34,241
Now!

24
00:03:34,313 --> 00:03:36,439
Toombs!

25
00:03:50,661 --> 00:03:54,119
Riddick.

26
00:03:55,534 --> 00:03:58,263
I don't know, Toombs.
Looks kinda tight.

27
00:03:58,337 --> 00:04:01,965
Not where I'm sittin'.
This is the biggest payday ever,

28
00:04:02,041 --> 00:04:05,100
So throw on a fresh pair of panties.
Let's get this right.

29
00:04:15,553 --> 00:04:19,922
<i>Three meters clearance port-side.
One and a half meters starboard.</i>

30
00:04:19,992 --> 00:04:22,482
We got a choke point comin' up.

31
00:04:35,006 --> 00:04:37,532
<i>What the shit was that?</i>

32
00:04:39,377 --> 00:04:42,506
Tags, you got eyes on Riddick?

33
00:04:42,581 --> 00:04:45,379
Tags?

34
00:04:48,953 --> 00:04:51,444
Jesus.

35
00:04:51,523 --> 00:04:54,458
He just ghosted two guys,
and I never even saw him.

36
00:04:56,127 --> 00:04:58,410
What do you think, Toombs?
I mean, maybe we oughta just...

37
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,929
I think you're my new gunner.

38
00:05:00,314 --> 00:05:02,122
Grab a Gat.

39
00:05:09,641 --> 00:05:11,699
Stay on top of him this time.

40
00:05:39,605 --> 00:05:43,268
<i>You made three mistakes.</i>

41
00:05:44,775 --> 00:05:48,302
First, you took the job.

42
00:05:48,379 --> 00:05:50,405
Second, you came light.

43
00:05:50,482 --> 00:05:55,078
<i>A four-man crew for me?
Fuckin' insulting.</i>

44
00:05:55,153 --> 00:05:58,282
<i>But the worst mistake you made...</i>

45
00:06:00,158 --> 00:06:02,319
<i>Empty gun rack.</i>

46
00:06:07,098 --> 00:06:10,067
- What's the bounty on my head?
- One mil.

47
00:06:12,804 --> 00:06:17,434
- One-point-five.
- What slam pays 1.5 for a convict?

48
00:06:17,509 --> 00:06:19,773
Private party.

49
00:06:19,845 --> 00:06:22,780
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Guy, guy! Easy! Anonymous.

50
00:06:22,848 --> 00:06:26,215
- That's what the sheet said.
- What planet?

51
00:06:27,586 --> 00:06:29,554
Helion Prime.

52
00:06:36,828 --> 00:06:39,763
Whoa. Where you going'?
Last question.

53
00:06:39,831 --> 00:06:43,494
And you better get this one right, merc.

54
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,468
Whose ship is this?

55
00:06:45,537 --> 00:06:48,232
Mine?

56
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,828
<i>Knew they'd come for me.</i>

57
00:07:10,896 --> 00:07:13,888
<i>Took 'em five years, but I knew.</i>

58
00:07:13,965 --> 00:07:18,629
<i>You don't expect these mercs
to have any honor, any code.</i>

59
00:07:20,405 --> 00:07:24,773
<i>But this new bounty from a holy man,</i>

60
00:07:24,843 --> 00:07:27,812
<i>a guy whose neck I saved...</i>

61
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,215
<i>Well, lesson learned.</i>

62
00:07:31,283 --> 00:07:34,013
<i>No such word as "friend. "</i>

63
00:07:34,086 --> 00:07:37,316
<i>It can only end bad
when you let someone get too close.</i>

64
00:07:38,523 --> 00:07:40,718
<i>Bad for them.</i>

65
00:07:43,461 --> 00:07:48,831
<i>So now it's back to all the brightness...
and everything I hate.</i>

66
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,734
<i>I wonder if she'll be there.</i>

67
00:08:02,547 --> 00:08:07,540
Act like an animal and I'm gonna slot you
up like one. This one is always in trouble.

68
00:08:07,619 --> 00:08:09,586
I knew it!
I smell it.

69
00:08:30,641 --> 00:08:32,336
Get in there!

70
00:08:58,102 --> 00:09:00,093
Can we shut the goddamn noise?

71
00:09:32,503 --> 00:09:36,405
<i>They say most of your brain
shuts down in cryosleep.</i>

72
00:09:36,474 --> 00:09:40,001
<i>Brain shuts down in cryosleep.</i>

73
00:09:40,078 --> 00:09:43,275
<i>- All but the primitive side.
- All but the primitive side.</i>

74
00:09:43,348 --> 00:09:45,646
<i>The animal side.</i>

75
00:09:45,717 --> 00:09:49,243
<i>All but the Furyan side.</i>

76
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:58,726
Some of us still remember the true
crime that happened here on Furya.

77
00:10:01,565 --> 00:10:04,227
And once you wake...

78
00:10:04,301 --> 00:10:07,065
truly wake...

79
00:10:09,473 --> 00:10:11,703
you'll remember too.

80
00:10:16,247 --> 00:10:20,014
<i>Helion Prime is on alert condition four.</i>

81
00:10:24,289 --> 00:10:29,852
<i>Unrecognized craft. You need to follow me
to Spaceport Six for security inspections.</i>

82
00:10:29,928 --> 00:10:33,159
<i>Hey! Do you hear me?</i>

83
00:10:33,231 --> 00:10:35,892
<i>Follow me to Spaceport Six now!</i>

84
00:11:25,449 --> 00:11:28,282
Imam, pray for us.

85
00:11:28,352 --> 00:11:31,617
<i>It was confirmed
two seasons back. Yes.</i>

86
00:11:31,689 --> 00:11:34,021
<i>They're coming here.
I mean, are we next?</i>

87
00:11:34,092 --> 00:11:36,083
<i>Militants storm...</i>

88
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:39,289
<i>Yes. But going to the underground
shelters if it happens...</i>

89
00:11:39,363 --> 00:11:41,559
<i>You're right.
That's what I thought too.</i>

90
00:11:41,632 --> 00:11:44,101
<i>Are you staying or leaving?</i>

91
00:11:44,169 --> 00:11:46,501
<i>It's the end of everything.
Everything!</i>

92
00:11:46,570 --> 00:11:50,063
<i>Well, my neighbours...
Half my street is gone.</i>

93
00:11:50,141 --> 00:11:52,040
What are we gonna do?
I don't know. I don't know.

94
00:11:52,109 --> 00:11:54,044
<i>Hood of the devil.
That's what someone called 'em.</i>

95
00:11:54,112 --> 00:11:56,204
Them? Who is them?
Some kind of new creature...

96
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:58,271
This is nonsense.
It's all nonsense.

97
00:11:58,349 --> 00:12:02,251
<i>So tall that it touches the clouds.</i>

98
00:12:02,319 --> 00:12:06,689
And there's nothing around this
statue, this colossus. Nothing left.

99
00:12:06,757 --> 00:12:08,987
It's their calling card.

100
00:12:19,471 --> 00:12:22,668
<i>Did you know all your doors were locked?</i>

101
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:30,112
<i>Five years ago,</i>

102
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:33,082
<i>I took two people off that planet...</i>

103
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:37,382
<i>A kid, Jack,
who everyone else thought was a boy,</i>

104
00:12:37,454 --> 00:12:40,150
<i>and a holy man...</i>

105
00:12:40,224 --> 00:12:42,159
<i>searching for New Mecca.</i>

106
00:12:45,697 --> 00:12:47,790
<i>Your wife...</i>

107
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,692
She's in the shower.

108
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:56,729
<i>I told one man...</i>

109
00:12:56,808 --> 00:12:59,971
where I might go.

110
00:13:00,045 --> 00:13:03,981
I showed trust to one man.

111
00:13:04,049 --> 00:13:07,540
Did I make a mistake, Imam?

112
00:13:07,618 --> 00:13:09,950
There is no simple answer.

113
00:13:10,021 --> 00:13:14,719
Whatever was said
was meant to give us a chance...

114
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:16,784
a fighting chance.

115
00:13:17,396 --> 00:13:21,029
Were it not for the threat of invasion,
I never would have betrayed you.

116
00:13:21,099 --> 00:13:24,830
<i>- I give you my word, Riddick.
- Riddick?</i>

117
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:27,861
Riddick!

118
00:13:30,775 --> 00:13:33,300
<i>And a daughter...</i>

119
00:13:34,746 --> 00:13:37,839
- No!
- Whose name would be...

120
00:13:37,915 --> 00:13:40,476
If you have issue with me,
you let it be with me.

121
00:13:40,551 --> 00:13:43,020
<i>- You need not know their names.
- Ziza.</i>

122
00:13:45,256 --> 00:13:47,155
My name is Ziza.

123
00:13:48,459 --> 00:13:50,394
Ziza.

124
00:13:52,097 --> 00:13:56,089
<i>- Cute kid.
- Did you really kill monsters?</i>

125
00:13:56,166 --> 00:13:58,692
The ones that were gonna
hurt my father?

126
00:14:00,538 --> 00:14:02,665
Such are our bedtime stories.

127
00:14:02,741 --> 00:14:05,436
Go, Ziza. Go on!

128
00:14:10,482 --> 00:14:14,612
So now who do I have to kill
to get this payday off my head?

129
00:14:30,501 --> 00:14:35,030
<i>It is said the comet
always precedes them...</i>

130
00:14:35,106 --> 00:14:37,597
these world-enders.

131
00:14:39,678 --> 00:14:41,612
The Coalsack planets are gone.

132
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:44,512
<i>Eight million settlers missing.</i>

133
00:14:44,582 --> 00:14:48,210
<i>The entire Aquilan System is gone too.</i>

134
00:14:48,285 --> 00:14:52,689
Helion Prime shares its sunlight
with all worlds nearby.

135
00:14:54,825 --> 00:14:59,525
If we fall, they fall.

136
00:14:59,597 --> 00:15:01,929
And after that...

137
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,163
My God,
how do I save my family?

138
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:12,338
<i>Have you heard anything I've said?</i>

139
00:15:14,646 --> 00:15:18,275
You said it's all circling the
drain... the whole universe.

140
00:15:18,348 --> 00:15:20,282
<i>- Right?
- That's right.</i>

141
00:15:29,294 --> 00:15:31,454
Had to end sometime.

142
00:15:49,046 --> 00:15:51,038
The one you want is now here.

143
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,434
And whose throat is this?

144
00:16:12,436 --> 00:16:17,101
If you cut my throat, I'll not be able to
rescind the offer that brought you here.

145
00:16:17,175 --> 00:16:19,699
Nor tell you why it's so vital
that you did come.

146
00:16:19,777 --> 00:16:22,679
The blade comes off
when the bounty comes off.

147
00:16:22,747 --> 00:16:26,376
This is Aereon,
an envoy from the Elemental race.

148
00:16:26,450 --> 00:16:28,817
She means you no harm.

149
00:16:32,723 --> 00:16:36,386
There are very few of us who have met
a Necromonger and lived to speak of it.

150
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:41,091
So when I choose to speak of it,
you should choose to listen.

151
00:16:41,165 --> 00:16:43,224
Necromonger.

152
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:48,602
It is the name that will convert
or kill every last human life...

153
00:16:48,673 --> 00:16:51,766
<i>unless the universe
can rebalance itself.</i>

154
00:16:53,710 --> 00:16:58,079
Maybe you should pretend like you're talkin'
to someone educated in the penal system.

155
00:16:58,149 --> 00:17:01,346
<i>In fact, don't pretend.</i>

156
00:17:01,419 --> 00:17:04,785
<i>Balance is everything
to elementals.</i>

157
00:17:04,856 --> 00:17:06,847
Water to fire.
Earth to air.

158
00:17:06,925 --> 00:17:09,257
<i>We have 33 different words for it.</i>

159
00:17:09,327 --> 00:17:13,923
But now we have only time
to speak of the balance of opposites.

160
00:17:13,998 --> 00:17:17,866
<i>There is a story, Riddick,
of young male Furyans...</i>

161
00:17:17,935 --> 00:17:20,461
strangled at birth...

162
00:17:20,538 --> 00:17:22,732
strangled with their own cords.

163
00:17:24,408 --> 00:17:27,105
When Aereon told this story
to the Helion leaders,

164
00:17:27,177 --> 00:17:29,271
I told her of you.

165
00:17:29,347 --> 00:17:32,441
- What do you know of your early years?
- Do you remember your home world?

166
00:17:32,517 --> 00:17:34,984
- Where it was?
- Have you met any others?

167
00:17:35,052 --> 00:17:37,043
Others like yourself.

168
00:17:39,691 --> 00:17:43,717
Sister, they don't know
what to do with just one of me.

169
00:17:43,794 --> 00:17:46,286
<i>Open up in there!</i>

170
00:17:46,364 --> 00:17:48,763
<i>- Stand back!
- Open up!</i>

171
00:17:48,832 --> 00:17:50,767
They are searching houses!

172
00:17:50,835 --> 00:17:53,827
They look for a man who came here
today. They think he might be a spy.

173
00:17:53,905 --> 00:17:56,236
- A spy?
- Did someone see him come here today?

174
00:17:56,307 --> 00:17:57,967
<i>- Did they?
- Lajjun, stop!</i>

175
00:17:58,041 --> 00:18:02,604
I will send them away.
But wait one minute, please.

176
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:05,842
<i>Will you wait one minute
to save worlds?</i>

177
00:18:07,551 --> 00:18:10,281
Not my fight.

178
00:18:10,355 --> 00:18:12,618
So, you will leave us
to our fate,

179
00:18:12,690 --> 00:18:15,021
<i>just like you did her.</i>

180
00:18:15,092 --> 00:18:18,323
<i>Break it down!</i>

181
00:18:20,098 --> 00:18:21,155
Get him!

182
00:18:21,232 --> 00:18:23,563
Come. Let us try to send them away.

183
00:18:27,038 --> 00:18:29,268
<i>Move it. Come on.
Leave us alone!</i>

184
00:18:31,509 --> 00:18:34,909
There is no one here!

185
00:18:34,979 --> 00:18:38,779
<i>You don't understand.
He can help us! He can help us!</i>

186
00:18:41,985 --> 00:18:43,976
<i>Go!</i>

187
00:18:49,327 --> 00:18:52,296
You're not afraid of the dark, are you?

188
00:19:12,684 --> 00:19:15,243
<i>- Get him!
- Where is he?</i>

189
00:19:15,319 --> 00:19:17,652
In there!

190
00:19:44,615 --> 00:19:47,106
You mentioned her.

191
00:19:47,184 --> 00:19:50,051
She, uh...

192
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:52,055
She went looking for you.

193
00:19:52,123 --> 00:19:55,523
People died.
She went to prison.

194
00:19:55,592 --> 00:19:59,426
I... I don't remember where.

195
00:20:00,431 --> 00:20:05,868
But it was a world so hot
you could not survive on the surface.

196
00:20:05,936 --> 00:20:09,428
- Crematoria.
- Young Jack.

197
00:20:09,507 --> 00:20:11,702
She thought of you
as her older brother.

198
00:20:11,776 --> 00:20:14,801
- She worshipped you.
- You were supposed to watch her.

199
00:20:15,946 --> 00:20:18,608
<i>She never forgave you...</i>

200
00:20:18,683 --> 00:20:22,050
for leaving just when
she needed you most.

201
00:20:22,119 --> 00:20:27,216
She needed to stay away
from me. You all do.

202
00:20:29,493 --> 00:20:31,962
Riddick.

203
00:20:33,697 --> 00:20:37,098
Are you gonna stop
the new monsters now?

204
00:20:50,048 --> 00:20:53,848
Furyans.
Defiant to the end.

205
00:21:31,621 --> 00:21:33,556
No, no.

206
00:21:33,624 --> 00:21:36,115
We go to the shelter.

207
00:21:36,194 --> 00:21:38,662
We take only ourselves.

208
00:21:59,817 --> 00:22:01,808
Stay close.

209
00:22:34,318 --> 00:22:36,877
<i>No!</i>

210
00:23:48,059 --> 00:23:50,686
<i>Flight leaders, get all squads
off the ground now.</i>

211
00:23:50,761 --> 00:23:53,594
<i>We have heavy inbound.</i>

212
00:23:54,698 --> 00:23:56,826
<i>Follow me in!</i>

213
00:24:15,051 --> 00:24:17,213
The next shelter.
This way!

214
00:24:17,288 --> 00:24:19,312
Yeah!

215
00:24:19,389 --> 00:24:21,755
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

216
00:24:42,812 --> 00:24:46,010
I'll see if it's safe.

217
00:24:51,222 --> 00:24:54,749
- Stay back!
- Come, Ziza.

218
00:25:12,576 --> 00:25:14,907
Come!

219
00:25:34,432 --> 00:25:36,456
You following me?

220
00:26:14,003 --> 00:26:16,062
Lajjun and Ziza!

221
00:26:16,139 --> 00:26:18,836
- When it's over.
- Let me go. I must get to my family!

222
00:26:18,908 --> 00:26:21,241
When it's over.

223
00:26:47,605 --> 00:26:49,765
<i>I borrowed a ship.</i>

224
00:26:49,839 --> 00:26:53,434
You can ride along,
if you don't mind riding with a convict.

225
00:26:53,511 --> 00:26:56,844
I thank you, but I must get
my family across the river.

226
00:26:56,914 --> 00:26:59,177
God willing, there is still
a shelter I can get them...

227
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:01,274
I'm sure God has his tricks,

228
00:27:01,351 --> 00:27:05,117
<i>but getting out of places
no one else can,</i>

229
00:27:05,188 --> 00:27:07,384
that's one of mine.

230
00:27:08,392 --> 00:27:10,451
Let's get your family.

231
00:27:13,062 --> 00:27:15,053
Aah!

232
00:27:44,595 --> 00:27:46,586
In here.

233
00:27:47,731 --> 00:27:50,097
Get in.

234
00:27:51,801 --> 00:27:53,996
Shh.

235
00:28:58,202 --> 00:29:00,796
<i>- Imam!
- Don't follow me.</i>

236
00:30:35,499 --> 00:30:38,331
There will be
an afterlife for me.

237
00:30:40,003 --> 00:30:41,937
Will there be for you?

238
00:31:59,883 --> 00:32:03,409
Let's go replenish the ranks.

239
00:32:16,265 --> 00:32:18,700
Never fails to inspire, does it?

240
00:32:18,769 --> 00:32:20,999
Each time a dynasty falls.

241
00:32:21,070 --> 00:32:24,598
Remember your place,
Dame Vaako.

242
00:32:24,675 --> 00:32:27,802
My place is at your side,
dear husband.

243
00:32:27,877 --> 00:32:30,004
From here till UnderVerse come.

244
00:32:54,437 --> 00:32:57,703
In this 'verse,

245
00:32:57,774 --> 00:33:01,836
life is antagonistic
to the natural state.

246
00:33:03,379 --> 00:33:08,443
<i>Here, humans in all
their various races...</i>

247
00:33:08,519 --> 00:33:11,646
are a spontaneous outbreak...

248
00:33:11,722 --> 00:33:13,916
an unguided mistake.

249
00:33:13,991 --> 00:33:15,982
Our purpose...

250
00:33:16,059 --> 00:33:19,893
is to correct that mistake.

251
00:33:21,098 --> 00:33:24,396
Because there is another 'verse...

252
00:33:24,467 --> 00:33:29,462
a 'verse where life
is welcomed and cherished.

253
00:33:29,540 --> 00:33:35,341
<i>A ravishing, ever-new place
called UnderVerse.</i>

254
00:33:36,579 --> 00:33:40,277
But the road to that 'verse...

255
00:33:40,349 --> 00:33:42,340
crosses over the threshold.

256
00:33:42,418 --> 00:33:45,512
Threshold!
Take us to the threshold!

257
00:33:45,588 --> 00:33:49,388
What you call... death.

258
00:33:49,459 --> 00:33:55,261
<i>So it is this 'verse
that must be cleansed of life,</i>

259
00:33:55,331 --> 00:33:59,598
so that UnderVerse
can populate and prosper.

260
00:34:02,172 --> 00:34:06,733
<i>Look around you.
Every Necromonger in this hall,</i>

261
00:34:06,809 --> 00:34:11,269
every one of the Legion Vast that just
swept aside your defenses in one night...

262
00:34:11,347 --> 00:34:14,077
was once like you.

263
00:34:14,151 --> 00:34:16,881
Fought as feebly as you.

264
00:34:17,955 --> 00:34:20,890
Every Necromonger
that lives today...

265
00:34:20,957 --> 00:34:23,084
is a convert.

266
00:34:23,160 --> 00:34:28,359
- There'll be no conversions!
- We all began as something else!

267
00:34:30,633 --> 00:34:35,071
It was hard for me to accept, too,
when I first heard these words.

268
00:34:35,138 --> 00:34:37,731
But I changed.

269
00:34:37,807 --> 00:34:40,140
I let them take away my pain.

270
00:34:40,209 --> 00:34:44,408
- You betrayed your faith!
- Just as you will change...

271
00:34:44,481 --> 00:34:49,941
<i>when you realize that the threshold
to the UnderVerse will be crossed...</i>

272
00:34:50,019 --> 00:34:54,184
<i>only by those who have
embraced the Necromonger faith.</i>

273
00:34:54,258 --> 00:34:57,385
For those of you
who will right now...

274
00:34:57,461 --> 00:35:01,522
drop to your knees
and ask to be purified.

275
00:35:01,597 --> 00:35:05,124
- We will not renounce our faith!
- No one here will do what you ask.

276
00:35:06,569 --> 00:35:08,002
It is unthinkable!

277
00:35:08,071 --> 00:35:13,441
<i>This is a world of many peoples,
many religions!</i>

278
00:35:13,510 --> 00:35:17,912
And we simply cannot
and will not be converted!

279
00:35:17,981 --> 00:35:20,778
Then I'll take your soul.

280
00:35:32,129 --> 00:35:34,689
<i>Join him...</i>

281
00:35:34,765 --> 00:35:37,961
Or join me.

282
00:35:57,888 --> 00:36:00,550
This is your one chance.

283
00:36:00,624 --> 00:36:03,091
Take the Lord Marshal's offer
and bow.

284
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:05,993
I bow to no man.

285
00:36:13,169 --> 00:36:15,194
He's not a man.

286
00:36:15,272 --> 00:36:18,935
He's the holy Half-Dead
who has seen the UnderVerse.

287
00:36:19,008 --> 00:36:21,499
Look, I'm not
with everyone here.

288
00:36:21,577 --> 00:36:24,171
But I will take a piece of him.

289
00:36:30,754 --> 00:36:32,745
A piece you will have.

290
00:37:00,751 --> 00:37:02,776
<i>Stop him!</i>

291
00:37:15,198 --> 00:37:17,631
Irgun. One of my best.

292
00:37:17,700 --> 00:37:20,169
If you say so.

293
00:37:23,874 --> 00:37:26,138
What do you think of this blade?

294
00:37:35,885 --> 00:37:38,252
I think it's a half-gram heavy
on the back end.

295
00:37:38,321 --> 00:37:40,289
In our faith,

296
00:37:40,356 --> 00:37:42,517
you keep what you kill.

297
00:37:49,800 --> 00:37:51,859
Are you familiar to me?

298
00:37:54,703 --> 00:37:58,196
Have we met
on some distant field?

299
00:37:59,376 --> 00:38:01,104
You'd think I'd remember.

300
00:38:02,646 --> 00:38:05,910
You'd think I would too.

301
00:38:05,981 --> 00:38:09,542
Take him before the Quasi-Deads.

302
00:38:16,526 --> 00:38:19,892
Perhaps the breeder
would do it...

303
00:38:19,963 --> 00:38:22,453
if somebody just asked him.

304
00:38:24,434 --> 00:38:26,834
It is a rare offer.

305
00:38:28,738 --> 00:38:31,707
A visit inside Necropolis.

306
00:38:33,310 --> 00:38:37,006
It's been a long time
since I smelled beautiful.

307
00:38:38,814 --> 00:38:40,941
Let me show you the way.

308
00:39:34,571 --> 00:39:36,903
Beautiful eyes.

309
00:39:36,972 --> 00:39:38,964
Come.

310
00:39:41,711 --> 00:39:45,807
The last six Lord Marshals
have called this home.

311
00:39:45,881 --> 00:39:48,146
Magnificent, isn't it?

312
00:39:48,218 --> 00:39:51,984
- I might have gone a different way.
- True of us all.

313
00:39:53,990 --> 00:39:58,086
<i>Converts receiving the mark
of the Necromonger.</i>

314
00:40:00,330 --> 00:40:03,595
They learn how one pain
can lessen another.

315
00:40:17,714 --> 00:40:19,705
There now.

316
00:40:21,383 --> 00:40:24,682
That is just... perfect.

317
00:40:28,057 --> 00:40:31,254
The more you resist them,

318
00:40:31,327 --> 00:40:33,693
the greater the damage will be.

319
00:40:36,265 --> 00:40:39,292
<i>A new one.</i>

320
00:40:39,368 --> 00:40:42,167
<i>You've brought us a new one.</i>

321
00:40:55,718 --> 00:40:58,448
Interesting breeder.

322
00:41:14,504 --> 00:41:17,131
<i>Making entry.</i>

323
00:41:17,207 --> 00:41:20,972
<i>This won't take long.</i>

324
00:41:21,044 --> 00:41:24,104
<i>We've entered his neocortex.</i>

325
00:41:24,180 --> 00:41:28,048
<i>- Ahh! The Riddick!
- Regress.</i>

326
00:41:28,118 --> 00:41:31,747
<i>Scanning fresh memories.</i>

327
00:41:31,821 --> 00:41:34,847
<i>Thoughts of someone called Jack.</i>

328
00:41:34,923 --> 00:41:36,823
Riddick!

329
00:41:38,694 --> 00:41:40,754
<i>She went to prison.</i>

330
00:41:41,897 --> 00:41:44,923
<i>Now we find thoughts of an Elemental.</i>

331
00:41:45,001 --> 00:41:48,164
<i>The one race that would slow
the spread of Necromongers.</i>

332
00:41:48,238 --> 00:41:50,502
<i>- Furyans.
- Furyans.</i>

333
00:41:55,845 --> 00:41:58,006
Where does he come from?

334
00:41:58,080 --> 00:42:02,575
Who are his people?
These are the things I need to know.

335
00:42:04,553 --> 00:42:07,455
<i>We find energy.</i>

336
00:42:08,792 --> 00:42:11,624
<i>You must settle your past.</i>

337
00:42:11,694 --> 00:42:16,655
<i>We find Furyan energy.</i>

338
00:42:16,732 --> 00:42:19,064
<i>- For all of us.
- He's Furyan!</i>

339
00:42:20,502 --> 00:42:22,595
<i>Furyan!</i>

340
00:42:24,274 --> 00:42:26,935
<i>A Furyan survivor!</i>

341
00:42:28,211 --> 00:42:33,944
<i>Look at our world, at the graves of those
who didn't escape 30 years ago.</i>

342
00:42:34,017 --> 00:42:36,484
<i>There is no future
until we settle our past...</i>

343
00:42:39,055 --> 00:42:42,115
<i>for all of us
who bear the mark.</i>

344
00:42:43,158 --> 00:42:45,957
<i>Kill the Furyan! Kill the Riddick!</i>

345
00:42:46,028 --> 00:42:48,997
<i>Kill the Riddick! Kill the Riddick!
Kill the Riddick!</i>

346
00:42:50,064 --> 00:42:52,260
Kill the Riddick.

347
00:43:25,502 --> 00:43:27,332
Who is this man?

348
00:43:29,205 --> 00:43:32,173
Find him. Whatever it takes. Find him!

349
00:44:06,975 --> 00:44:11,970
Let me guess.
A five-man crew this time.

350
00:44:12,048 --> 00:44:14,345
Couple of things
you could have done better.

351
00:44:18,687 --> 00:44:23,318
First, trash the locator beacon
inside my ship... the one you jacked.

352
00:44:23,392 --> 00:44:26,760
<i>And second... and this is really
the more important part...</i>

353
00:44:26,830 --> 00:44:30,060
dust my dick
when you get the chance.

354
00:44:30,133 --> 00:44:33,863
- Any questions?
- Yeah.

355
00:44:36,406 --> 00:44:38,033
What took you so long?

356
00:44:45,347 --> 00:44:47,577
Let's go, big boy.

357
00:45:00,263 --> 00:45:04,597
In and out, unsuspected and undetected.
Damn, I love a good smash-and-grab.

358
00:45:04,667 --> 00:45:07,227
Not so fast. Not so fast.

359
00:45:07,303 --> 00:45:09,736
Dickheads.
We're pickin' up fields here.

360
00:45:09,805 --> 00:45:12,740
<i>Unknown fields detected on hull.</i>

361
00:45:12,809 --> 00:45:16,336
I knew it. Here it comes.
This is some kind of scan.

362
00:45:16,412 --> 00:45:18,403
I don't know.
Readin' our BTUs, maybe?

363
00:45:18,481 --> 00:45:21,972
- Let's drop one.
- Dropping.

364
00:45:29,993 --> 00:45:31,984
<i>Decoy launched.</i>

365
00:45:37,800 --> 00:45:40,769
<i>- Preparing to engage ion drive.
- So,</i>

366
00:45:40,836 --> 00:45:44,738
where do we drop
your merc-killin' ass?

367
00:45:44,807 --> 00:45:47,138
<i>Who's gonna pay
the most for you now?</i>

368
00:45:47,209 --> 00:45:50,941
- Butcher Bay?
- Butcher Bay.

369
00:45:51,013 --> 00:45:53,778
Ten minutes every other day
on the dog run.

370
00:45:53,850 --> 00:45:56,818
Protein waffles aren't bad.

371
00:45:56,885 --> 00:46:00,754
Hey, how 'bout Ursa Luna?
Nice little double-max prison.

372
00:46:00,823 --> 00:46:05,225
They keep a cell open for me...
just in case I drop in.

373
00:46:05,294 --> 00:46:07,229
<i>You know the problem
with these joints now?</i>

374
00:46:07,296 --> 00:46:10,265
Health clubs
for waffle-eatin' pussies.

375
00:46:10,332 --> 00:46:13,062
Maybe we should think about
uppin' our game here a little bit.

376
00:46:13,135 --> 00:46:15,502
Think about someplace
truly diabolical.

377
00:46:15,571 --> 00:46:17,562
What the hell is he thinkin' now?

378
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:20,164
<i>He's thinkin' a triple-max prison.</i>

379
00:46:20,243 --> 00:46:23,609
<i>A no-daylight slam.
Only three of 'em left in this system...</i>

380
00:46:23,680 --> 00:46:28,013
two of 'em outta range for a shitty little
under cutter like this one with no legs.

381
00:46:28,084 --> 00:46:31,611
Leavin' just... one...

382
00:46:31,687 --> 00:46:34,622
Crematoria.

383
00:46:34,687 --> 00:46:37,484
That is what you had in mind,
right, Toombs?

384
00:46:37,560 --> 00:46:40,039
Hey, how does he know where we're goin',
and we don't?

385
00:46:40,510 --> 00:46:41,229
Dope it out.

386
00:46:41,263 --> 00:46:42,377
I hate this run.

387
00:46:42,689 --> 00:46:44,330
Just do it!

388
00:46:44,740 --> 00:46:46,761
Don't know about this
new crew of yours.

389
00:46:46,836 --> 00:46:48,959
They seem a bit skittish.

390
00:46:49,280 --> 00:46:53,765
Probably shouldn't tell 'em
what happened to the last crew.

391
00:47:01,484 --> 00:47:05,977
You know, you supposed
to be some slick-shit killer.

392
00:47:06,055 --> 00:47:08,580
Now look at you...

393
00:47:08,658 --> 00:47:11,821
all back-of-the-bus
and shit.

394
00:47:48,397 --> 00:47:51,060
<i>I say we attack Helion Two next.</i>

395
00:47:51,133 --> 00:47:53,068
Take it straight
into their teeth.

396
00:47:53,135 --> 00:47:56,537
It'll cost you 20,000 heads, five
warrior ships. Nothing more, I swear it.

397
00:47:56,606 --> 00:47:59,939
While I do prize brute force,

398
00:48:00,008 --> 00:48:03,136
this approach
is perhaps more artful.

399
00:48:03,211 --> 00:48:06,044
Start at the end.

400
00:48:06,115 --> 00:48:08,106
Go straight to Helion Five,

401
00:48:08,184 --> 00:48:10,379
the last planet
in the system.

402
00:48:10,452 --> 00:48:13,080
We approach from the night side.

403
00:48:13,156 --> 00:48:16,124
<i>Remove these cannon first,</i>

404
00:48:16,191 --> 00:48:19,024
then attack
the larger placements at speed.

405
00:48:19,095 --> 00:48:21,892
<i>We'll catch them on their rear flank.
And in ten days' time,</i>

406
00:48:21,964 --> 00:48:26,298
<i>the rest of those worlds
will tumble before us.</i>

407
00:48:26,368 --> 00:48:28,700
You see, as with most,
their blind spot...

408
00:48:28,771 --> 00:48:31,068
is right behind them.

409
00:48:33,142 --> 00:48:36,702
I've located an ion trail
which leads off-world.

410
00:48:36,778 --> 00:48:39,475
Then you should be
off-world, Vaako.

411
00:48:39,548 --> 00:48:42,142
I've deployed a tracker team.
One of the best.

412
00:48:42,218 --> 00:48:45,948
Wherever Riddick has gone,
you lens him out and cleanse him.

413
00:48:46,937 --> 00:48:47,684
You.

414
00:48:47,688 --> 00:48:50,859
You want me to take a
frigate for one breeder?

415
00:48:50,993 --> 00:48:53,051
Don't question it, Vaako!

416
00:48:54,964 --> 00:48:58,160
Take it on faith.

417
00:49:01,336 --> 00:49:04,738
He's always been unsettled around you...

418
00:49:04,807 --> 00:49:06,832
the Lord Marshal.

419
00:49:06,908 --> 00:49:09,810
Unsteady.

420
00:49:09,879 --> 00:49:13,542
Perhaps because he knows
he's half the warrior you are.

421
00:49:13,615 --> 00:49:16,676
<i>Some say he's too artistic
for the job.</i>

422
00:49:18,187 --> 00:49:20,814
I wouldn't be surprised
if someone promoted him soon...

423
00:49:20,890 --> 00:49:23,825
<i>to full dead.</i>

424
00:49:26,229 --> 00:49:28,162
Take care what you say.

425
00:49:28,231 --> 00:49:31,131
Should I say it softly?

426
00:49:31,200 --> 00:49:34,169
So it sounds more
like conspiracy?

427
00:49:34,236 --> 00:49:38,071
Oh, why is it that when anyone breathes
about the demise of him on the throne...

428
00:49:38,140 --> 00:49:40,803
everyone assumes
a conspiracy?

429
00:49:42,511 --> 00:49:45,879
Why isn't that
just prudent planning?

430
00:49:45,948 --> 00:49:48,472
When he is ready,
he will name a successor.

431
00:49:48,551 --> 00:49:50,644
Who?

432
00:49:50,720 --> 00:49:54,986
Toal? Scales? The Purifier?

433
00:49:55,057 --> 00:49:57,388
None of them...

434
00:49:57,459 --> 00:50:00,223
with the strength,
the dignity,

435
00:50:00,296 --> 00:50:04,392
of Lord Vaako.

436
00:50:04,466 --> 00:50:06,696
You can keep what you kill.

437
00:50:06,769 --> 00:50:10,033
- Stop.
- That is the Necromonger way.

438
00:50:10,106 --> 00:50:13,667
I said... stop.

439
00:50:13,743 --> 00:50:17,109
His death will come in due time
and not a moment sooner.

440
00:50:17,580 --> 00:50:18,283
Why?

441
00:50:18,287 --> 00:50:21,776
Because I serve him.
We all serve him. It's called fidelity.

442
00:50:21,810 --> 00:50:23,010
It's called stupidity.

443
00:50:32,093 --> 00:50:34,084
Well, finally some attention.

444
00:50:47,008 --> 00:50:50,877
You have such greatness in you.

445
00:50:50,946 --> 00:50:53,073
If only you could see it like I do.

446
00:50:55,952 --> 00:50:57,977
You know what I want?

447
00:50:59,622 --> 00:51:03,649
Today I came up behind him
in perfect silence and he knew.

448
00:51:03,725 --> 00:51:06,160
I wanna go down
in Necropolis.

449
00:51:08,064 --> 00:51:10,055
Right now.

450
00:51:10,131 --> 00:51:15,160
His half-dead soul sensed I was
behind him. He sees everything.

451
00:51:15,238 --> 00:51:17,432
When no one is looking...

452
00:51:17,506 --> 00:51:20,066
when no one's around...

453
00:51:20,142 --> 00:51:22,406
I'm gonna get down on my knees...

454
00:51:24,146 --> 00:51:27,582
while you sit on the throne.

455
00:51:49,805 --> 00:51:53,638
- How unexpected.
- An Elemental.

456
00:51:53,709 --> 00:51:57,303
<i>- Here?
- One of the captives.</i>

457
00:51:57,379 --> 00:52:00,314
<i>And why, after 30 years,</i>

458
00:52:00,383 --> 00:52:02,613
should it be you?

459
00:52:02,685 --> 00:52:05,084
He doesn't regard her
as a captive, though.

460
00:52:05,153 --> 00:52:07,952
<i>Elementals...
they talk of neutrality,</i>

461
00:52:08,024 --> 00:52:10,015
<i>but they're all witches
and spies.</i>

462
00:52:10,091 --> 00:52:13,026
<i>Why else would they
come and go like the wind?</i>

463
00:52:13,095 --> 00:52:17,122
But where has he gone?
Where is the Furyan hiding now?

464
00:52:17,198 --> 00:52:20,133
You be the good warrior.

465
00:52:20,202 --> 00:52:23,102
Go after this Riddick.

466
00:52:23,171 --> 00:52:26,801
I'll find out why the Lord Marshal
is so threatened by him.

467
00:53:26,102 --> 00:53:30,037
<i>Do you know
you grind your teeth at night?</i>

468
00:53:31,841 --> 00:53:33,569
Sexy.

469
00:53:49,792 --> 00:53:52,225
<i>Destination reached.</i>

470
00:53:52,294 --> 00:53:54,227
<i>Unlocking manual controls.</i>

471
00:53:54,296 --> 00:53:57,662
All right. I make 700 degrees
on the day side,

472
00:53:57,732 --> 00:53:59,700
300 below on the night side.

473
00:53:59,769 --> 00:54:02,738
Let's not get caught in the sun.

474
00:54:02,805 --> 00:54:05,238
If I owned this place and hell,

475
00:54:05,307 --> 00:54:08,298
I'd rent this place out
and live in hell.

476
00:54:17,053 --> 00:54:19,452
<i>- Blue angle... good.
- Stand by.</i>

477
00:54:20,955 --> 00:54:22,946
<i>And...</i>

478
00:54:23,024 --> 00:54:24,959
<i>Plotted course good.</i>

479
00:54:25,026 --> 00:54:27,426
Hit it!

480
00:54:27,495 --> 00:54:31,330
<i>Angle of approach, not good.</i>

481
00:54:38,673 --> 00:54:41,370
<i>Look, Ma. No hands!</i>

482
00:55:15,810 --> 00:55:17,745
Party poppers!

483
00:55:40,169 --> 00:55:42,535
I think I shit myself.

484
00:55:43,772 --> 00:55:46,935
Skittish, Toombs. Very skittish.

485
00:56:08,464 --> 00:56:10,397
Comfy?

486
00:56:27,850 --> 00:56:31,216
When the ride's over,

487
00:56:31,287 --> 00:56:33,847
your goggles are mine.

488
00:57:02,417 --> 00:57:05,477
Four-way split!

489
00:57:15,798 --> 00:57:18,095
29.4 kilometers.

490
00:57:26,609 --> 00:57:30,943
So, this is Riddick.

491
00:57:55,604 --> 00:57:59,631
What in the bowels of Christ
are you talkin' about, 700K?

492
00:57:59,707 --> 00:58:01,607
Don't take this one, boss.

493
00:58:01,676 --> 00:58:04,975
See? Anatoli here
has a nose for trouble.

494
00:58:05,046 --> 00:58:07,412
And this one, this Riddick guy...

495
00:58:07,482 --> 00:58:09,575
Big, big trouble.

496
00:58:09,651 --> 00:58:12,780
So, 700,000 is good money.

497
00:58:12,854 --> 00:58:16,620
I'd take the money, Toombs.

498
00:58:24,332 --> 00:58:28,861
<i>The guild pays us a caretaker's fee
for each prisoner each year.</i>

499
00:58:28,937 --> 00:58:32,964
We pay mercs 20% of that total fee
based on a certain life expectancy.

500
00:58:33,042 --> 00:58:34,669
<i>How's about this?</i>

501
00:58:34,743 --> 00:58:37,678
You open that safe you got hidden
behind the console there,

502
00:58:37,745 --> 00:58:41,876
show me the real books,
then we figure out my cut.

503
00:58:41,950 --> 00:58:43,941
Then I'll be on my way.

504
00:58:48,823 --> 00:58:52,191
Open my books.
This is what you suggest?

505
00:58:57,231 --> 00:58:59,222
Wasn't a suggestion.

506
00:59:17,086 --> 00:59:21,818
<i>These are dangerous days,
if you believe the talk.</i>

507
00:59:22,825 --> 00:59:25,850
- Talk?
- About dead planets.

508
00:59:25,928 --> 00:59:29,055
About some ghost army.

509
00:59:29,131 --> 00:59:31,792
About them.

510
00:59:31,867 --> 00:59:35,303
"Them"?

511
00:59:52,086 --> 00:59:54,021
I'll run the numbers again.

512
00:59:54,089 --> 00:59:56,182
It takes a couple of days,
probably,

513
00:59:56,258 --> 00:59:59,658
so you can stay as my guest.

514
00:59:59,727 --> 01:00:01,662
At least here, we are all safe.

515
01:00:01,729 --> 01:00:05,028
<i>- Yes?
- Yes, boss.</i>

516
01:00:05,100 --> 01:00:07,499
I'll give it a day.

517
01:00:09,838 --> 01:00:11,964
One.

518
01:00:50,412 --> 01:00:52,345
<i>There are inmates...</i>

519
01:00:52,414 --> 01:00:55,144
<i>and there are convicts.</i>

520
01:00:55,216 --> 01:00:58,675
A convict has a certain code.

521
01:00:58,754 --> 01:01:02,689
And he knows to show
a certain respect.

522
01:01:03,758 --> 01:01:06,283
<i>An inmate, on the other hand,</i>

523
01:01:06,361 --> 01:01:08,885
pulls the pin on his fellow man.

524
01:01:08,964 --> 01:01:11,363
<i>Does the guards' work for them.</i>

525
01:01:11,432 --> 01:01:14,026
Brings shame...

526
01:01:14,102 --> 01:01:16,468
To the game.

527
01:01:18,473 --> 01:01:21,443
So, which are you gonna be?

528
01:01:21,510 --> 01:01:24,035
Me?

529
01:01:26,147 --> 01:01:28,446
I'm just passin' through.

530
01:01:34,256 --> 01:01:36,417
Welcome to Crematoria.

531
01:01:42,597 --> 01:01:45,031
Should I go for the sweet spot?

532
01:01:45,100 --> 01:01:48,729
Left of the spine, fourth lumbar down,
the abdominal aorta.

533
01:01:48,803 --> 01:01:51,203
What a gusher.

534
01:01:53,542 --> 01:01:55,533
How do I get eyes like that?

535
01:01:55,611 --> 01:01:57,977
You gotta kill a few people.

536
01:01:58,046 --> 01:02:00,207
Did that.

537
01:02:00,281 --> 01:02:02,113
Did a lot of that.

538
01:02:03,718 --> 01:02:05,984
And then you gotta get sent to a slam.

539
01:02:06,085 --> 01:02:07,485
One where they tell you
you'll never see daylight again?

540
01:02:07,555 --> 01:02:11,151
Only there wasn't any doctor here who could
shine my eyes, not even for 20 menthol Kools.

541
01:02:11,225 --> 01:02:13,318
Was there anything
you said that was true?

542
01:02:16,097 --> 01:02:19,328
What are you gonna do, huh?
Go for the sweet spot?

543
01:02:19,401 --> 01:02:22,767
Remember who
you're talkin' to, Jack.

544
01:02:24,506 --> 01:02:27,839
Jack's dead.
She was weak.

545
01:02:29,010 --> 01:02:31,479
She couldn't cut it.

546
01:02:44,626 --> 01:02:46,787
The name's Kyra now.

547
01:02:46,861 --> 01:02:48,830
And I'm a new animal.

548
01:03:25,100 --> 01:03:29,763
They can be quite a test,
these deep runs...

549
01:03:31,606 --> 01:03:33,767
tests of our inner selves.

550
01:03:36,111 --> 01:03:38,477
Don't you find that true?

551
01:03:42,428 --> 01:03:44,452
Some men do.

552
01:03:45,863 --> 01:03:48,388
<i>Just being so far from the armada,</i>

553
01:03:48,466 --> 01:03:54,336
the mind can start to fill
with strange thoughts, doubts.

554
01:03:54,406 --> 01:03:57,341
Don't you ever have doubts, Vaako?

555
01:04:00,778 --> 01:04:03,269
- Doubts?
- About the campaign.

556
01:04:04,283 --> 01:04:06,443
About Lord Marshal.

557
01:04:08,453 --> 01:04:12,823
First and always,
I am a Necromonger commander.

558
01:04:13,892 --> 01:04:18,988
So if you're here to test my loyalty,
you succeed only in testing my patience.

559
01:04:19,064 --> 01:04:22,658
Oh, no.
No, that's not why I'm here at all.

560
01:04:44,089 --> 01:04:46,785
<i>I'm so glad I could
steal you away for a moment.</i>

561
01:04:46,859 --> 01:04:49,258
Doesn't it strike you odd?

562
01:04:49,327 --> 01:04:51,955
<i>Here we have
the current Lord Marshal...</i>

563
01:04:52,031 --> 01:04:56,127
<i>destroying entire societies,
and yet he can't bring himself...</i>

564
01:04:56,200 --> 01:05:00,160
to kill one
stranded Elemental.

565
01:05:00,238 --> 01:05:02,173
Why is that?

566
01:05:03,374 --> 01:05:05,309
You don't pray to our god.

567
01:05:05,377 --> 01:05:07,937
You pray to no god, I hear.

568
01:05:08,013 --> 01:05:11,004
Elementals... we calculate.

569
01:05:12,084 --> 01:05:14,017
Don't we all.

570
01:05:14,086 --> 01:05:17,988
But now let's have first things first.

571
01:05:18,057 --> 01:05:21,287
What of Riddick? In truth,
I don't know where he went.

572
01:05:21,359 --> 01:05:24,294
In truth, I'm more interested
in where he came from.

573
01:05:26,432 --> 01:05:28,662
Watch your step.

574
01:05:28,734 --> 01:05:31,430
I've always wondered,

575
01:05:31,502 --> 01:05:34,097
does an air Elemental fly?

576
01:05:34,173 --> 01:05:36,164
<i>Now do me a favour.</i>

577
01:05:36,240 --> 01:05:40,200
Calculate the odds of you
getting off this planet alive...

578
01:05:40,278 --> 01:05:42,269
and now cut them in half.

579
01:05:43,716 --> 01:05:45,649
No, we can't fly.

580
01:05:45,718 --> 01:05:48,185
But we glide very well.

581
01:05:48,252 --> 01:05:51,051
<i>Save your threats, Necromonger.</i>

582
01:05:52,124 --> 01:05:55,685
I would have told you about Riddick
for the asking.

583
01:05:55,760 --> 01:05:59,560
It concerns a foretelling,
a prediction now more than 30 years old.

584
01:05:59,631 --> 01:06:03,930
<i>A young warrior
once consulted a seer.</i>

585
01:06:04,002 --> 01:06:09,064
<i>He was told a child would be born
on the planet Furya... a male child...</i>

586
01:06:09,140 --> 01:06:13,544
<i>who would someday
cause the warrior's downfall.</i>

587
01:06:13,611 --> 01:06:17,207
<i>Cause his untimed death.</i>

588
01:06:18,216 --> 01:06:23,176
Furya? Furya's a ruined world.
No life to speak of.

589
01:06:23,254 --> 01:06:24,812
For good reason.

590
01:06:24,890 --> 01:06:29,883
This young warrior
mounted an attack on Furya,

591
01:06:29,961 --> 01:06:33,055
killing all young males
he could find,

592
01:06:33,131 --> 01:06:37,227
even strangling some
with their birth cords.

593
01:06:37,301 --> 01:06:40,100
An artful stroke,
wouldn't you say?

594
01:06:42,006 --> 01:06:46,033
So this warrior, the one who tried to
outwit the prediction, would later become...

595
01:06:46,111 --> 01:06:48,135
That's why he worries.

596
01:06:48,213 --> 01:06:50,203
...our Lord Marshal.

597
01:06:51,816 --> 01:06:53,807
Which would make
the man-child...

598
01:06:53,885 --> 01:06:56,354
He worries he missed
killing that child in its crib.

599
01:06:56,421 --> 01:06:58,412
...Riddick.

600
01:07:15,439 --> 01:07:17,600
<i>- That's why it's so vital to him.
- Wait.</i>

601
01:07:17,676 --> 01:07:20,075
<i>- It's about a prophecy.
- Wait! Wait!</i>

602
01:07:23,115 --> 01:07:25,106
Are you there?

603
01:07:28,653 --> 01:07:31,053
You do what your lord asks.

604
01:07:31,122 --> 01:07:34,785
You cleanse Riddick for him,
and in doing so...

605
01:07:34,859 --> 01:07:38,260
you prove your undying loyalty.

606
01:07:38,330 --> 01:07:43,961
And perhaps then
he'll finally let down his guard.

607
01:08:26,959 --> 01:08:28,484
<i>Still here, I see?</i>

608
01:08:28,561 --> 01:08:32,293
I've been here 18 years.
See this?

609
01:08:34,367 --> 01:08:40,203
I remember how gorgeous she was.
Well, gorgeous in a certain light.

610
01:08:40,272 --> 01:08:43,173
And now,
for the goddamn death of me,

611
01:08:43,243 --> 01:08:45,369
I cannot remember her name.

612
01:08:45,579 --> 01:08:48,012
Feeding time!

613
01:08:52,385 --> 01:08:56,378
We're here for the rest
of our unnatural lives.

614
01:09:04,396 --> 01:09:06,092
Here they come!

615
01:09:11,404 --> 01:09:15,271
Whatever you do,
don't make eye contact.

616
01:10:14,434 --> 01:10:15,923
Aaah!

617
01:11:41,020 --> 01:11:43,011
It's an animal thing.

618
01:11:53,931 --> 01:11:57,526
<i>Check her for me.
She's always got a blade somewhere.</i>

619
01:12:24,262 --> 01:12:27,561
Hyah!

620
01:12:57,296 --> 01:13:00,288
<i>I don't think
she likes being touched.</i>

621
01:13:02,467 --> 01:13:06,767
I'd take my wounded and go
while you still can.

622
01:13:12,244 --> 01:13:16,305
Is there a name for this
private little world of yours, huh?

623
01:13:16,382 --> 01:13:21,182
What happens there
when we don't just run away?

624
01:13:21,252 --> 01:13:23,721
<i>You'll kill us... with a soup cup?</i>

625
01:13:23,788 --> 01:13:26,120
Tea, actually.

626
01:13:26,190 --> 01:13:28,124
What's that?

627
01:13:30,695 --> 01:13:34,187
I'll kill you with my teacup.

628
01:13:45,944 --> 01:13:49,276
You know the rule. They aren't dead
if they're still on the books.

629
01:13:49,347 --> 01:13:52,511
Mmm.

630
01:14:09,967 --> 01:14:11,458
Come on.

631
01:14:34,325 --> 01:14:36,418
Death by teacup.

632
01:14:40,598 --> 01:14:43,033
Damn. Why didn't I think of that?

633
01:14:43,101 --> 01:14:45,934
<i>I didn't come to play
"Who's the Better Killer?"</i>

634
01:14:46,003 --> 01:14:49,404
But it's my favourite game.
Haven't you heard?

635
01:14:49,475 --> 01:14:51,909
- I heard you came lookin' for me.
- Is that all?

636
01:14:51,976 --> 01:14:54,638
Then you missed the good part.

637
01:14:54,713 --> 01:14:56,976
Hooked up with some mercs
outta Lupus Five.

638
01:14:57,048 --> 01:15:00,415
Said they'd take me on,
teach me the trade, give me a good cut.

639
01:15:01,720 --> 01:15:03,347
They slaved me out, Riddick.

640
01:15:03,422 --> 01:15:06,550
Do you know what that could do to you
when you're that age?

641
01:15:06,624 --> 01:15:10,220
- When you're 12 years old?
- I told you to stay in New Mecca.

642
01:15:10,294 --> 01:15:12,820
Did you not listen?

643
01:15:12,897 --> 01:15:15,092
I had mercs on my neck.

644
01:15:15,167 --> 01:15:17,601
I'll always have mercs on my neck.

645
01:15:17,668 --> 01:15:21,332
I spent five years on a frozen heap
just to keep 'em away from you.

646
01:15:22,341 --> 01:15:25,275
And you go and sign up
with the same fake badges...

647
01:15:25,343 --> 01:15:27,334
that wanted to cut you up
and use you for bait.

648
01:15:27,412 --> 01:15:31,780
What are you pitching, Riddick?
That you cuttin' out was a good thing?

649
01:15:31,850 --> 01:15:35,285
That you had my ass covered
from halfway across the universe?

650
01:15:35,354 --> 01:15:37,948
You signed with mercs.

651
01:15:41,693 --> 01:15:44,525
There was nobody else around.

652
01:15:58,476 --> 01:16:01,605
Let's pop the cork.
Get some fresh air.

653
01:16:38,717 --> 01:16:40,810
So they do go topside...

654
01:16:42,220 --> 01:16:44,984
to swap out air.

655
01:16:45,056 --> 01:16:47,490
Interesting.

656
01:16:47,559 --> 01:16:49,288
Who the hell are you?

657
01:16:51,229 --> 01:16:54,629
When it happens, it'll happen fast.

658
01:16:54,699 --> 01:16:58,136
<i>Stay on my leg when I cut fence
or stay here...</i>

659
01:16:58,203 --> 01:17:00,194
for the rest of your unnatural life.

660
01:17:00,271 --> 01:17:04,140
Nobody outs this place.
Nobody.

661
01:17:10,181 --> 01:17:12,513
<i>He ain't "nobody. "</i>

662
01:17:26,565 --> 01:17:30,934
<i>Good news first.
Talked things over with my amigos here.</i>

663
01:17:31,002 --> 01:17:34,234
We'll cut you in for 775K.

664
01:17:36,675 --> 01:17:38,734
Well, all right.

665
01:17:38,810 --> 01:17:41,176
What's the bad news?
They close the local whorehouse?

666
01:17:43,847 --> 01:17:47,614
<i>No. The bad news is worse than that.
Much worse.</i>

667
01:17:47,685 --> 01:17:52,713
Our pilot, he saw this.
It crossed a shipping lane.

668
01:17:56,260 --> 01:17:59,752
<i>Any idea what this might be?</i>

669
01:18:03,367 --> 01:18:06,359
Never saw nothin' like it.

670
01:18:06,436 --> 01:18:10,133
<i>This ship charts back
to Helion Prime.</i>

671
01:18:10,207 --> 01:18:13,734
You know, Anatoli's
got a nose for trouble,

672
01:18:13,811 --> 01:18:17,872
<i>and he thinks
trouble follows you here.</i>

673
01:18:19,984 --> 01:18:24,318
<i>Look. We dusted our tracks
and got the hell outta there.</i>

674
01:18:24,387 --> 01:18:27,379
There is no way
we didn't lose them.

675
01:18:28,525 --> 01:18:31,427
"Them"?

676
01:18:36,867 --> 01:18:40,097
This is my prisoner. Mine.

677
01:18:40,171 --> 01:18:42,162
Nobody else's.

678
01:18:42,239 --> 01:18:44,570
And I want my money now.

679
01:18:44,641 --> 01:18:46,734
<i>So...</i>

680
01:18:46,811 --> 01:18:49,244
you stole a prisoner...

681
01:18:49,312 --> 01:18:51,303
from "them"?

682
01:19:58,548 --> 01:20:00,743
No.

683
01:20:00,818 --> 01:20:03,912
<i>Riddick. No!</i>

684
01:20:09,126 --> 01:20:13,118
Shoulda taken the money, Toombs.

685
01:21:09,086 --> 01:21:11,610
You gonna kill me?

686
01:21:44,954 --> 01:21:47,150
<i>Mercs.</i>

687
01:21:48,626 --> 01:21:51,060
Some guards here,
but this can't be all of them.

688
01:21:52,296 --> 01:21:55,595
<i>Check their slots in the back...
and be careful.</i>

689
01:21:55,665 --> 01:21:57,656
<i>Don't bother.</i>

690
01:21:57,734 --> 01:22:00,135
Guards ain't there.

691
01:22:00,204 --> 01:22:02,934
<i>They figured out the Necros
are comin' for me.</i>

692
01:22:03,007 --> 01:22:06,169
Plan was to clean the bank,
ghost the mercs,

693
01:22:06,243 --> 01:22:08,177
break wide through the tunnel.

694
01:22:08,244 --> 01:22:11,976
And then somebody got a lucky shot off
with this rocket launcher here...

695
01:22:12,048 --> 01:22:14,039
and took out the sled.

696
01:22:14,118 --> 01:22:18,248
Guards took off on foot but rigged
the door so no one could follow.

697
01:22:19,323 --> 01:22:23,918
<i>They'll take the one ship in the hangar
and leave everyone else here to die.</i>

698
01:22:23,993 --> 01:22:27,360
How come you know all this shit?

699
01:22:27,431 --> 01:22:29,455
You weren't even here.

700
01:22:30,467 --> 01:22:32,593
'Cause it was my plan.

701
01:22:38,309 --> 01:22:40,868
I shoulda taken the money.

702
01:22:47,618 --> 01:22:49,847
Riddick!

703
01:23:00,431 --> 01:23:03,559
<i>What is this?
What is he thinking?</i>

704
01:23:03,633 --> 01:23:06,602
<i>- Once that sun comes up...
- We'll last five minutes.</i>

705
01:23:06,669 --> 01:23:10,628
Five minutes. We ain't gonna last
30 seconds out there.

706
01:23:10,708 --> 01:23:12,699
It'll light you up like a match.

707
01:23:17,280 --> 01:23:21,445
20-mile buffer zone
and 30 klicks to the hangar.

708
01:23:23,619 --> 01:23:26,885
30 klicks over that terrain?

709
01:23:39,403 --> 01:23:43,566
It's moving in the right direction.
We could make it.

710
01:23:43,940 --> 01:23:46,636
Stay behind the night,

711
01:23:46,709 --> 01:23:49,007
ahead of the sun.

712
01:23:49,079 --> 01:23:51,410
There's gonna be one speed...

713
01:23:53,516 --> 01:23:55,507
mine.

714
01:23:57,787 --> 01:23:59,948
<i>If you can't keep up, don't step up.</i>

715
01:24:00,022 --> 01:24:01,957
You'll just die.

716
01:25:06,088 --> 01:25:07,851
<i>Riddick?</i>

717
01:25:09,926 --> 01:25:11,917
Riddick?

718
01:25:15,297 --> 01:25:17,288
Riddick?

719
01:25:21,803 --> 01:25:25,330
Go, go! Go on! Go! Climb here!

720
01:25:25,408 --> 01:25:28,070
Climb! Go! Go, go, go!

721
01:25:53,769 --> 01:25:55,600
Boss!

722
01:25:59,441 --> 01:26:01,409
<i>Up there.</i>

723
01:26:01,476 --> 01:26:03,672
- Take a look.
- Because Anatoli says so?

724
01:26:03,745 --> 01:26:06,839
Because his nose says so.

725
01:26:24,133 --> 01:26:26,693
There's nothin' up here.

726
01:26:28,770 --> 01:26:30,204
Oh, shit.

727
01:26:39,981 --> 01:26:42,542
Riddick.

728
01:26:42,618 --> 01:26:46,247
<i>They're heading right for the volcano
fields. They're going for our ship!</i>

729
01:26:46,321 --> 01:26:48,915
No chance do they get to
the hangar first. No chance!

730
01:27:00,703 --> 01:27:02,897
Next one! Next hole!
We'll catch 'em there!

731
01:27:30,832 --> 01:27:33,131
<i>No more run for you.</i>

732
01:27:38,341 --> 01:27:41,776
Where did the big guy go?

733
01:27:47,516 --> 01:27:49,484
Ohh...

734
01:28:14,543 --> 01:28:16,271
Close it!

735
01:28:47,877 --> 01:28:50,709
What was that?
You don't care if you live or die?

736
01:28:50,779 --> 01:28:53,806
If I kill them first, not really.

737
01:28:55,450 --> 01:28:57,543
Maybe I do.

738
01:28:57,619 --> 01:28:59,610
Keep moving!

739
01:29:56,945 --> 01:30:00,039
<i>Kyra?</i>

740
01:30:00,115 --> 01:30:02,141
- Kyra!
- What?

741
01:30:02,217 --> 01:30:04,879
Get that ass moving!

742
01:30:42,556 --> 01:30:45,423
Riddick?

743
01:30:50,097 --> 01:30:54,091
Remember what I said
about not caring if I lived or died?

744
01:30:57,771 --> 01:30:59,966
You knew I was kidding, right?

745
01:31:03,243 --> 01:31:04,734
"One speed. "

746
01:31:25,365 --> 01:31:27,231
Temperature differential.

747
01:31:27,302 --> 01:31:29,793
Your rope.

748
01:31:29,870 --> 01:31:32,236
It's too late.
We're never gonna make it.

749
01:31:32,306 --> 01:31:34,400
Your rope! Gimme your rope!

750
01:31:35,543 --> 01:31:37,601
And your water. All of it!

751
01:31:38,645 --> 01:31:42,104
Stay in the shadow of the mountain.
Don't wait for me. Run!

752
01:31:54,028 --> 01:31:56,394
Riddick!

753
01:32:07,441 --> 01:32:08,841
Aaah!

754
01:32:40,341 --> 01:32:42,275
Where the hell is that hangar?

755
01:32:47,281 --> 01:32:51,082
<i>There it is.</i>

756
01:32:53,087 --> 01:32:57,352
<i>Listen.</i>

757
01:33:22,684 --> 01:33:25,618
Let me guess. Necros.

758
01:33:25,686 --> 01:33:28,883
And a whole lotta Necro firepower.

759
01:33:28,957 --> 01:33:32,256
<i>Shit! I hate not being the bad guys.</i>

760
01:34:00,320 --> 01:34:05,452
I figure we got three minutes before the sun
hits us again, burns out this whole valley.

761
01:34:05,526 --> 01:34:08,222
- Wait.
- We gonna do this or not?

762
01:34:08,296 --> 01:34:10,195
Just wait.

763
01:34:15,269 --> 01:34:17,430
Ellen.

764
01:34:18,873 --> 01:34:21,841
Her name was Ellen.
I never really forgot.

765
01:34:39,127 --> 01:34:41,721
Aaah! Boss!

766
01:34:52,973 --> 01:34:56,841
- Remember that favourite game of yours?
- "Who's the Better Killer?"

767
01:34:58,980 --> 01:35:02,972
- Let's play.
- Come on!

768
01:35:21,269 --> 01:35:22,963
On the right!

769
01:35:30,477 --> 01:35:32,275
Watch out!
Behind you!

770
01:35:32,346 --> 01:35:34,109
<i>Kyra!</i>

771
01:36:30,169 --> 01:36:32,195
Sybar!

772
01:37:33,732 --> 01:37:35,667
<i>No!</i>

773
01:37:57,690 --> 01:37:59,921
Aaah!

774
01:38:17,610 --> 01:38:20,306
<i>Get up. Get up!</i>

775
01:38:20,379 --> 01:38:22,347
<i>Please get up.</i>

776
01:38:35,662 --> 01:38:37,323
<i>So,</i>

777
01:38:39,231 --> 01:38:42,029
you can kneel.

778
01:38:59,485 --> 01:39:01,976
<i>I think you know now.</i>

779
01:39:03,656 --> 01:39:06,091
I think you know
who tore Furya apart.

780
01:39:09,428 --> 01:39:12,955
This mark carries the anger
of an entire race.

781
01:39:18,305 --> 01:39:20,397
But it's going to hurt.

782
01:41:38,243 --> 01:41:40,473
Kyra?

783
01:41:44,350 --> 01:41:47,284
<i>I was supposed to
deliver a message to you...</i>

784
01:41:49,254 --> 01:41:51,552
if Vaako failed to kill you.

785
01:41:53,459 --> 01:41:56,223
A message from
the Lord Marshal himself.

786
01:41:58,131 --> 01:42:01,623
He tells you to stay away from Helion,
stay away from him,

787
01:42:02,968 --> 01:42:05,096
and in return,
you'll be hunted no more.

788
01:42:12,078 --> 01:42:14,910
But Vaako will most likely
report you as dead.

789
01:42:16,315 --> 01:42:18,580
So this is your chance.

790
01:42:18,651 --> 01:42:22,417
Your chance to do
what no man has ever done.

791
01:42:22,489 --> 01:42:24,480
The girl.

792
01:42:25,492 --> 01:42:27,686
Where will they take her?

793
01:42:44,676 --> 01:42:48,008
We all began... as something else.

794
01:42:52,251 --> 01:42:56,847
I've done... unbelievable things...

795
01:42:57,856 --> 01:43:00,619
in the name of a faith
that was never my own.

796
01:43:02,528 --> 01:43:06,486
And he'll do to her
what he did to me.

797
01:43:12,738 --> 01:43:17,368
The Necromonger in me
warns you not to go back.

798
01:43:18,709 --> 01:43:21,338
But the Furyan in me...

799
01:43:24,883 --> 01:43:26,611
hopes you won't listen.

800
01:43:32,457 --> 01:43:37,120
God knows... I've dreamed of it.

801
01:44:38,323 --> 01:44:41,189
<i>I have lost a Purifier...</i>

802
01:44:42,427 --> 01:44:47,227
<i>but I have gained
a first among commanders.</i>

803
01:44:48,232 --> 01:44:50,860
It is overdue, isn't it...

804
01:44:50,936 --> 01:44:53,632
that we acknowledge
your many accomplishments,

805
01:44:53,705 --> 01:44:55,865
<i>your steady faith,</i>

806
01:44:55,940 --> 01:45:01,470
and above all,
your unflinching loyalty.

807
01:45:09,221 --> 01:45:12,713
Obedience without question.
Loyalty till UnderVerse come.

808
01:45:15,226 --> 01:45:17,217
Well done, Vaako.

809
01:45:18,497 --> 01:45:22,091
This is a day of days.

810
01:45:41,886 --> 01:45:44,412
Look more pleased, Vaako.

811
01:45:46,190 --> 01:45:49,591
You have killed his enemy...

812
01:45:49,660 --> 01:45:51,423
and his suspicions.

813
01:45:51,495 --> 01:45:52,609
I should have brought back his head.

814
01:45:53,300 --> 01:45:56,297
You saw him unbreathing.
You saw him dead on the ground.

815
01:45:56,339 --> 01:45:59,359
Riddick was no common breeder.
In a heartbeat he dropped 20 of my men.

816
01:45:59,437 --> 01:46:03,396
All mysteries are not miracles,
not even in this religion.

817
01:46:05,910 --> 01:46:08,504
And if you say it is certain,
then it is certain,

818
01:46:08,580 --> 01:46:11,878
and we've already said it,
haven't we?

819
01:46:14,519 --> 01:46:16,510
We have.

820
01:46:20,292 --> 01:46:22,816
<i>Now, tell me if it's true.</i>

821
01:46:22,894 --> 01:46:27,126
Tell me the Furyan is gone, and I can close
this campaign without hearing his bootsteps.

822
01:46:28,633 --> 01:46:30,624
If he is dead,

823
01:46:31,803 --> 01:46:33,828
I sense I'm not far
from the same fate,

824
01:46:34,905 --> 01:46:36,839
being of no further use here.

825
01:46:37,909 --> 01:46:40,968
Shouldn't I tell you
that Riddick is still alive?

826
01:46:41,046 --> 01:46:42,842
Don't try me, Aereon.

827
01:46:42,913 --> 01:46:45,178
I could plough you under
with the rest of Helion Prime.

828
01:46:45,249 --> 01:46:47,582
No one really knows the future.

829
01:46:47,651 --> 01:46:51,452
Then tell me the odds
that Vaako met with success,

830
01:46:51,522 --> 01:46:53,513
that I will now be the one...

831
01:46:53,591 --> 01:46:56,493
who can carry his people across
the threshold into UnderVerse,

832
01:46:56,561 --> 01:46:58,552
where they shall begin true life.

833
01:46:58,629 --> 01:47:00,928
Tell me what I want to hear, Aereon,

834
01:47:00,999 --> 01:47:05,095
and maybe
I'll save your home world... for last.

835
01:47:09,940 --> 01:47:12,431
- The odds are good...
- That?

836
01:47:12,510 --> 01:47:15,071
That you will reach the UnderVerse...

837
01:47:18,283 --> 01:47:20,274
<i>soon.</i>

838
01:47:58,656 --> 01:48:00,454
Ascension protocol!

839
01:48:00,525 --> 01:48:04,222
We still have numbers out there, Lord
Marshal... sweep teams, recon ships.

840
01:48:04,296 --> 01:48:06,355
They would be hard-pressed
to make it back...

841
01:48:11,169 --> 01:48:14,968
Get my armada off the ground!

842
01:49:16,499 --> 01:49:20,061
- You mean on Helion?
- I mean here, on this very ship!

843
01:49:20,136 --> 01:49:24,437
Could you be wrong?
Mind fabricates fear.

844
01:49:24,508 --> 01:49:28,774
Could you be wrong? Not so wrong
as you when you left him alive!

845
01:49:28,846 --> 01:49:30,779
It's twice a mistake.

846
01:49:30,847 --> 01:49:34,113
Not only your failure,
but now the report of success.

847
01:49:34,184 --> 01:49:37,778
How do we salvage this? How? How?

848
01:49:37,855 --> 01:49:40,414
Lord Marshal's got to be warned.

849
01:49:40,490 --> 01:49:42,425
You will never see the UnderVerse!

850
01:49:43,760 --> 01:49:45,887
He will kill us both
before our due time.

851
01:49:49,033 --> 01:49:50,966
I say give Riddick his chance.

852
01:49:55,805 --> 01:49:58,400
If he is half of what you think,

853
01:49:58,475 --> 01:50:00,499
he can at least wound the Lord Marshal...

854
01:50:00,578 --> 01:50:03,069
and that is when you must act.

855
01:50:03,146 --> 01:50:05,512
Just to take his place?
Just to keep what I kill?

856
01:50:05,582 --> 01:50:08,312
- That is the Necromonger way.
- It is not enough!

857
01:50:08,385 --> 01:50:11,149
Then you do it for the faith!

858
01:50:11,221 --> 01:50:13,950
If he has fear, he has weakness.

859
01:50:14,024 --> 01:50:15,957
If he has weakness, Vaako...

860
01:50:17,994 --> 01:50:20,155
He is unworthy of lordship.

861
01:50:21,164 --> 01:50:23,497
We do it for all Necromongers.

862
01:50:25,002 --> 01:50:27,162
Protect the faith.

863
01:50:27,236 --> 01:50:30,262
This can still be a day of days,

864
01:50:30,341 --> 01:50:32,434
but the timing...

865
01:50:32,508 --> 01:50:35,501
must be flawless.

866
01:50:57,333 --> 01:51:00,860
Final protocol.
Execute on my order.

867
01:51:35,772 --> 01:51:38,037
Go inside.

868
01:51:39,142 --> 01:51:41,133
Are they leaving now?

869
01:51:41,211 --> 01:51:43,975
Ziza! Go inside!

870
01:52:35,732 --> 01:52:37,997
<i>We found this Lensor dead.</i>

871
01:52:40,571 --> 01:52:44,028
<i>Show me his last sight.</i>

872
01:52:56,419 --> 01:52:58,115
Commander Toal.

873
01:52:58,187 --> 01:53:00,178
He won't escape twice.

874
01:54:52,568 --> 01:54:55,696
Stay your weapons!

875
01:54:57,138 --> 01:54:59,129
He came for me.

876
01:55:25,901 --> 01:55:28,267
<i>Consider this:</i>

877
01:55:33,142 --> 01:55:37,238
<i>If you fall here now,</i>

878
01:55:37,312 --> 01:55:39,247
you'll never rise.

879
01:55:39,314 --> 01:55:42,443
<i>But if you choose another way...</i>

880
01:55:43,618 --> 01:55:45,779
<i>the Necromonger way...</i>

881
01:55:45,855 --> 01:55:48,379
<i>you'll die in due time...</i>

882
01:55:48,457 --> 01:55:52,187
and rise again in the UnderVerse.

883
01:56:01,837 --> 01:56:04,031
Go to him.

884
01:56:11,546 --> 01:56:13,537
It hurts...

885
01:56:14,550 --> 01:56:16,814
at first.

886
01:56:16,885 --> 01:56:20,481
But after a while, the pain
goes away, just as they promise.

887
01:56:22,892 --> 01:56:25,417
- Are you with me, Kyra?
- There's a moment...

888
01:56:25,493 --> 01:56:27,894
when you can almost
see the UnderVerse through his eyes.

889
01:56:29,231 --> 01:56:31,994
It makes it sound perfect...

890
01:56:32,068 --> 01:56:34,002
a place where anyone
can start over.

891
01:56:34,070 --> 01:56:36,537
Are you with me, Kyra?

892
01:56:49,084 --> 01:56:51,519
Convert now...

893
01:56:51,587 --> 01:56:53,748
or fall forever.

894
01:56:58,526 --> 01:57:00,790
You killed everything I know.

895
01:57:05,935 --> 01:57:07,128
Vaako.

896
01:57:09,238 --> 01:57:11,502
Not yet.

897
01:57:23,052 --> 01:57:26,020
Been a long time
since I've seen my own blood.

898
01:58:44,300 --> 01:58:47,292
These are his last moments.

899
01:59:06,888 --> 01:59:09,722
Give me your soul.

900
01:59:14,730 --> 01:59:18,165
Fuck you!

901
02:00:23,464 --> 02:00:25,729
You're not the one to bring me down.

902
02:00:44,720 --> 02:00:47,449
Now! Kill the beast
while he's wounded!

903
02:01:05,138 --> 02:01:08,164
Help me, Vaako. Kill him.

904
02:01:15,816 --> 02:01:17,147
Vaako?

905
02:01:21,823 --> 02:01:23,814
Forgive me.

906
02:01:23,891 --> 02:01:25,586
Flawless.

907
02:01:56,457 --> 02:01:58,925
No.

908
02:02:04,999 --> 02:02:08,400
No-o-o!

909
02:02:08,468 --> 02:02:11,562
Now what would be
the odds of that?

910
02:02:24,552 --> 02:02:27,145
I thought you were dead.

911
02:02:29,390 --> 02:02:31,949
Are you with me, Kyra?

912
02:02:34,028 --> 02:02:36,588
I was always with you.

913
02:02:38,932 --> 02:02:40,923
I was.

914
02:04:04,484 --> 02:04:06,816
You keep what you kill.
